1679 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 438 0 R
/E (In the modern digital era, effective financial management has become a necessity for individuals to monitor their income, control expenses, and plan budgets efficiently. With the increasing number of daily transactions and diverse spending categories, managing finances manually becomes time- consuming and error-prone. To address this challenge, the Expense Tracker System has been developed as a web-based application using the MERN stack \(MongoDB, Express.js, React.js, and Node.js\). The primary objective of this system is to provide a simple, secure, and efficient platform for personal financial management through digital automation. The Expense Tracker System enables users to maintain a clear and organized record of their financial transactions. Users can add income details, record expenses, and classify transactions into various categories such as food, travel, shopping, healthcare, utilities, and entertainment. This structured categorization helps users analyze their spending habits and identify areas where expenses can be reduced. The system also includes)
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
1680 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 438 0 R
/E (a budget management module, which allows users to set monthly or category-wise budget limits based on their financial goals and income levels. A key feature of the system is its real-time budget monitoring mechanism. The application continuously tracks total expenses and compares them with the predefined budget limits. When expenses exceed or approach the allocated budget, the system automatically generates an alert notification to inform the user. This alert-based functionality encourages responsible financial behavior and helps users avoid overspending by providing timely warnings and insights.The backend of the Expense Tracker System is implemented using Node.js and Express.js, which manage server-side logic, user authentication, and secure API communication. MongoDB is used as the database to store user profiles, income records, expense details, budgets, and category information in a scalable and flexible manner. The frontend of the application is developed using React.js, offering a responsive, interactive, and user-friendly interface that ensures a smooth user experience across various devices and screen sizes. This project demonstrates the effective integration of frontend and backend technologies in a full- stack development environment. It highlights concepts such as modular architecture, real-time data handling, secure data management, and alert-based monitoring.)
/Pg 70 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
